1528e4be (816 1793299325256 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f381") (src . "code-suggest: JSX in plain JavaScript is refused by position, not by text\n\nThe ecmascript scan refused JSX with a text pass over the whole file: the\nfirst \"<\" followed by \"/\" or \"/\" followed by \">\", whitespace between. It\nfired on markup in strings and comments, on regexes such as /a/>b, and\nmissed a self-close whose \"/\" and \">\" a line comment separates. The test\nnow runs inside ecmascript-judgments, on every live reading, under the\nplain-JavaScript profile only. A \"<\" in code where an operand is\nexpected falls the file back with reason opener: no JavaScript\nexpression begins with \"<\". A \"/\" read as a division (not \"/=\") whose\nnext significant character, past whitespace, comments and line ends, is\n\">\" falls it back with reason self-close: \">\" begins no divisor. Strings,\ncomments, template text and regex bodies are not code and refuse\nnothing. jsx-pass is removed.\n\nThe limit is stated in the scan's header and the README: JSX whose\noutermost opener sits where an operator is expected (a statement start\nafter \")\" or \"}\", after debugger, yield, await or of) can pass, and the\nfile may then be cut inside it; the blocks still join to the file. The\ncost: a file is refused when some live reading meets either rule, such\nas a regex beginning with \">\" where an operator is expected. TypeScript\nis not tested.\n\n- code-suggest.sc: the two rules and next-sig in ecmascript-judgments;\n  jsx-pass removed; the header.\n- languages.sc: the profile's comment.\n- README: the reasons opener and self-close; the limit and the cost.\n- Tests: ecmascript-scan (the opener and self-close rows, markup in\n  strings, comments, templates and regexes, the limit's passing shapes,\n  the cost's shapes); import-symbols (IS4c reads opener at the <div>);\n  tree-round-trip (the two reasons); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 521))))
